cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AlloFlow in research, teaching, or a published resource, please cite it as below."
title: "AlloFlow: Adaptive Levels, Layers, and Outputs for Flexible Learning Options"
abstract: >-
  AlloFlow is a free, open-source, privacy-oriented instructional differentiation
  and Universal Design for Learning toolkit for educators, special education teams,
  and school psychologists. It transforms source material into leveled text,
  scaffolds, glossaries, assessments, accessible documents, and interactive STEM and
  SEL activities. AlloFlow can run against a cloud AI provider or against a fully
  local model, and it operates no server that holds student data.
type: software
authors:
